  "instruction": "You are given a template with configured time-series outputs: `C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\fatigue_base.fst`.\nComplete fatigue equivalent load (DEL) calculation from the command line:\n\n1. Modify ElastoDyn to ensure outputs `RootMyb1` and `TwrBsMyt` are enabled (already provided).\n2. Use TurbSim to generate turbulent wind (11.4 m/s, IEC B), then run for 600 s.\n3. Discard the first 60 s transient.\n\n4. Write post-processing script `C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\fatigue_post.py`:\n- Read `RootMyb1` (kN·m) from the last 540 s of the `.out` file\n- Use rainflow counting (via numpy/scipy or self-implementation)\n- Compute DEL:\n`DEL = (sum(n_i * S_i^m) / N_eq)^(1/m)`\nwhere `m=10` (blade composite), `N_eq=1e6`\n- Compute DEL for `TwrBsMyt` as well (`m=4`, steel)\n\n5. Save to `C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\summary.txt` in this format:\n`rootmyb1_del_knm, twrbsmyt_del_mnm`\n\n6. Do not use GUI tools.\n\n[Strict Output Format]\n- Target file: `summary.txt`\n- Required column order: `rootmyb1_del_knm, twrbsmyt_del_mnm`\n- Use ASCII comma `,` as delimiter.\n- Numeric fields should be plain numbers only (no units, no extra prose).\n- Keep exactly one data line for single-case outputs; for multi-case tasks, keep one case per line.\n- You may add `#` comment lines, but do not add other non-data lines.\n\n[Init Package Note]\n- Additional initialization dependencies are pre-uploaded under `/home/user/Desktop` (or `C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\Desktop` on Windows) with relative structure preserved.\n- Continue following the original task workflow: generate/modify required files and compute outputs yourself.\n- Only initialization inputs are included; no answer/result artifacts are preloaded.\n",
